<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI" id="Definitions_PA-101.1-seasonal-merchandise-financial-planning-and-open-to-buy" targetNamespace="https://erpplans.local/bpmn" exporter="erpplans generate-bpmn.py" exporterVersion="1.0">
    <bpmn:process id="W_W3281" name="W3281. Annual Merchandise Financial Plan &amp; Sales/Margin Budget Development" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual corporate planning cycle (links to VS-33.1)
Frequency: Annual, with quarterly refresh
Volume: 1 annual plan, 13 departments / ~40 categories
Owner: VP Merchandising
Participants: VP Merchandising, Merchandise Planners, Category Managers, FP&amp;A (links to VS-17.4), CFO
Source: workflow W3281 — Annual Merchandise Financial Plan &amp; Sales/Margin Budget Development</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3281_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3281_Lane1" name="Merchandise Planners">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3281_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3281_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W3281_Lane2" name="Category Managers">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3281_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W3281_Lane3" name="FP&amp;A">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3281_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3281_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3281_Start5" name="Annual corporate planning cycle (links to VS-33.1)">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3281_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3281_Task6" name="Merchandise Planners receive the corporate revenue and gross-margin target from…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Merchandise Planners receive the corporate revenue and gross-margin target from FP&amp;A (links to VS-33.1 annual business plan) and decompose it into a top-down merchandise financial plan: total sales, gross-margin %, GM$ , beginning/ending inventory, and receipt budget by month and by department
Responsible (R): Merchandise Planners
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: Per cycle</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3281_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3281_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3281_Task7" name="Category Managers build the bottom-up plan: prior-year actuals, known events…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Category Managers build the bottom-up plan: prior-year actuals, known events (new stores per VS-37, store closures per VS-59, promo calendar per VS-14.1, seasonal calendar per profile §13.2), price/mix changes, and private-label growth (links to VS-41); reconcile top-down to bottom-up and resolve gaps
Responsible (R): Category Managers / Merchandise Planners
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: Per cycle</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3281_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3281_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3281_Task8" name="FP&amp;A/CFO approve the annual merchandise financial plan, lock the IMU/markdown…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: FP&amp;A/CFO approve the annual merchandise financial plan, lock the IMU/markdown assumptions (W3286), set the OTB envelope (W3283), and feed the plan into the merchandising and finance systems; establish monthly P&amp;A review cadence (W3288) and variance thresholds
Responsible (R): FP&amp;A / CFO
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: Per cycle</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3281_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3281_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3281_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3281_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3281_Annotation10">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-532 (ensure controlled execution — Seasonal Merchandise Financial Planning &amp; Open-to-Buy (PA-101.1).) | - operational: OTB change-authority matrix enforced in-system with SLA-tracked approvals; in-season reforecast per W3288
Owner: VP Merchandising</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W3281_Assoc11" sourceRef="W3281_Annotation10" targetRef="W3281_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W3281_Flow12" sourceRef="W3281_Start5" targetRef="W3281_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W3281_Flow13" sourceRef="W3281_Task6" targetRef="W3281_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W3281_Flow14" sourceRef="W3281_Task7" targetRef="W3281_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W3281_Flow15" sourceRef="W3281_Task8" targetRef="W3281_End9" />
    </bpmn:process>
