    <bpmn:process id="W_W3286" name="W3286. Gross-Margin Plan, Initial Markup (IMU) &amp; Markdown-Margin Modeling" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual plan; pricing/cost change; markdown decision
Frequency: Annual + periodic
Volume: ~40 categories, ~35,000 SKUs
Owner: Merchandise Planner
Participants: Merchandise Planner, Category Managers, Pricing (links to VS-01.2/VS-57), FP&amp;A (links to VS-17.4), Rebate (links to VS-39)
Source: workflow W3286 — Gross-Margin Plan, Initial Markup (IMU) &amp; Markdown-Margin Modeling</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3286_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3286_Lane1" name="Merchandise Planner">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3286_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3286_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3286_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W3286_Lane2" name="Category Managers">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3286_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3286_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3286_Start4" name="Annual plan; pricing/cost change; markdown decision">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3286_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3286_Task5" name="Merchandise Planner set the IMU plan (gross margin before markdown) by category…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Merchandise Planner set the IMU plan (gross margin before markdown) by category using cost (incl. landed cost per VS-02.2/VS-87), retail, vendor rebates (links to VS-39), and mix; model the maintained margin = IMU − markdown % − shrink (links to VS-23) to hit the 28–32% gross-margin target
Responsible (R): Merchandise Planner / Pricing
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: Periodic</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3286_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3286_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3286_Task6" name="Category Managers model price/cost/mix scenarios: vendor cost increase (links…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Category Managers model price/cost/mix scenarios: vendor cost increase (links to VS-03.3), SRP change (links to VS-01.2), bundle pricing (links to VS-92), promo elasticity (links to VS-58), and import FX impact (links to VS-18.3); select the mix that preserves maintained margin
Responsible (R): Category Managers / Pricing
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: Periodic</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3286_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3286_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3286_Task7" name="Merchandise Planner/FP&amp;A reconcile planned vs actual maintained margin, isolate…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Merchandise Planner/FP&amp;A reconcile planned vs actual maintained margin, isolate drivers (IMU, markdown, shrink, mix, FX), and feed variance to weekly P&amp;A (W3288) and monthly finance close (links to VS-17.1)
Responsible (R): Merchandise Planner / FP&amp;A
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: Periodic</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3286_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3286_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3286_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3286_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
